{#- Two static browser toolboxes, each an nginx serving prebuilt files —
   no state, no volumes, no secrets. Everything runs in the browser.

   cyberchef: GCHQ's image is nginx-unprivileged (uid 101, listens on
   8080, pid/temp files in /tmp), so the podman defaults fit as they are:
   read-only root, no capabilities.

   it_tools: built on the stock nginx image — master as root (inside its
   own user namespace), listening on 80, workers as nginx (101). With the
   default read-only root and ALL caps dropped it needs:
     tmpfs /var/cache/nginx — nginx's temp dirs (the image's entrypoint
       scripts only touch files they can write and skip the rest);
     cap_add NET_BIND_SERVICE for :80, SETUID/SETGID to drop the workers
       to nginx, CHOWN to hand them the temp dirs, KILL to signal them.
   Tags: IT-Tools publishes <date>-<commit> (renovate.json rule).

   host_port: published on the minion; homepage items point here.
   podman: spec overrides per container (keys: formulas/podman README). #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'cyberchef': {
        'image': 'ghcr.io/gchq/cyberchef',
        'tag': '11.6.0',
        'container_name': 'cyberchef',
        'host_port': 8081,
        'container_port': 8080,
        'podman': {},
    },
    'it_tools': {
        'image': 'ghcr.io/corentinth/it-tools',
        'tag': '2024.10.22-7ca5933',
        'container_name': 'it-tools',
        'host_port': 8082,
        'container_port': 80,
        'tmpfs': ['/var/cache/nginx'],
        'cap_add': ['CHOWN', 'KILL', 'NET_BIND_SERVICE', 'SETGID', 'SETUID'],
        'podman': {},
    },
} %}
{%- set toolbox = salt['pillar.get']('toolbox:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
